========================================================================
             THE MASTER CLOUD ENGINEER'S GIT & GITHUB CHEAT SHEET
========================================================================

------------------------------------------------------------------------
💻 COMMANDS RUN ONLY ON YOUR LOCAL MACHINE (LAPTOP)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
git init
-> Installs the Git engine locally inside your current folder.

git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "your.email@example.com"
-> Registers your engineering signature on your laptop for every save.

git status
-> Your main project dashboard. (Red = untracked changes, Green = staged).

git add .
-> Loads all your modified files onto the local staging launchpad.

git commit -m "your commit message"
-> Clicks the camera shutter to lock a permanent snapshot into local history.

git log --oneline
-> Reads a clean, compressed list of all snapshots stored on your local timeline.

git checkout -b <branch-name>
-> Constructs and steps into a new, isolated playground branch on your laptop.

git checkout main
-> Jumps your workspace back onto the local master timeline.

git branch -d <branch-name>
-> Safely destroys a local playground branch from your hard drive once finished.

git branch -a
-> Lists all local and remote branches so you see what exists everywhere.

git stash
-> Locks your current uncommitted local edits in a drawer to clear your screen.

git stash pop
-> Opens the stash drawer and pulls your loose edits back onto your screen.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
🔀 COMMANDS RUN ON YOUR LAPTOP THAT TALK TO THE CLOUD (GITHUB)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
git remote add origin <GITHUB_REPO_URL>
-> Tells your laptop the exact web address of your remote cloud locker.

git clone <GITHUB_REPO_URL>
-> Downloads an entire cloud project to your laptop for the very first time.

git push origin <branch-name>
-> Uploads your local branch timeline and files up into the GitHub cloud vault.

git pull origin main
-> Downloads the latest master blueprints from GitHub to update your computer.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
🛡️ EMERGENCY BUTTONS (UNDOING MISTAKES ON YOUR LAPTOP)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
git restore --staged <filename>
-> Un-stages a file. Takes a green file off the launchpad back to red status.

git reset --soft HEAD~1
-> Erases the last commit record, but keeps your files open and green to edit.

git reset --hard HEAD
-> Wipes out all uncommitted edits. Warps your files back to the last clean save.

git revert HEAD
-> Run this, then run "git push". Creates an opposite commit to cancel out a 
   mistake that you already pushed live to GitHub without breaking the team.

git reflog
-> Opens the master black-box diary to rescue deleted commits or bad resets.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
☁️ OPERATIONS HANDLED ONLY IN YOUR BROWSER (GITHUB.COM)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Create Repository
-> Done on GitHub.com to provision a brand new, empty cloud storage folder.

Fork
-> Copies someone else's repository into your personal cloud account to practice.

Open Pull Request (PR)
-> Invites your team leads to review your branch code before it hits production.

Merge Pull Request
-> Fuses your feature branch into the remote main branch (triggers cloud deploys).

------------------------------------------------------------------------
🔒 THE INVISIBLE SECURITY SHIELD
------------------------------------------------------------------------
.gitignore (A text file named exactly this inside your project folder)
-> Write the names of files inside it (like passwords, API keys, and .env). 
   Git reads this and guarantees it will never track or upload them to the cloud.
